1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,800
I have been an organic farmer in Maine since the 1970s.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:07,060
And no one can tell me or the other farmers here today

3
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:10,520
that we can't grow food without all of these toxic chemicals.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:18,060
Over 140,000 family farms will close this year and nobody is talking about it.

5
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,680
140,000, guys.

6
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:21,860
Why is this happening?

7
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:26,220
Well, in the 1990s, Monsanto, later acquired by Bayer,

8
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:28,800
introduced something called Roundup Ready Crops,

9
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:32,640
which are crops that are genetically engineered to resist glyphosate,

10
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:35,980
which is the key ingredient in their weed killer, Roundup.

11
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:41,280
This then led to a massive explosion in the use of glyphosate in factory farming,

12
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:46,040
with now about 60% of total crops being treated with this pesticide.

13
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:49,480
The only problem is that Roundup causes cancer,

14
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,320
and Bayer has already had to pay tens of billions of dollars to settle these cases,

15
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:57,540
which obviously is not ideal for corporate profits.

16
00:00:57,540 --> 00:01:00,980
In fact, Bayer is pushing a case in the Supreme Court right now

17
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:05,240
that blocks people from suing them if they get cancer from Roundup.

18
00:01:05,460 --> 00:01:10,660
And the Trump administration is backing Bayer's bid to curb these Roundup lawsuits.

19
00:01:11,020 --> 00:01:12,000
And for the farmers who say,

20
00:01:12,260 --> 00:01:15,360
no, no, we don't want to chemicalize our food supply,

21
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,100
Bayer has methodically driven them one by one out of business,

22
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:23,300
with the help of President Barack Obama.

23
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:30,400
What has gotten us to this point is the mergers and consolidations of ag input suppliers.

24
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:33,180
In 2015, Monsanto and Bayer merged.

25
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:37,060
They were competing against each other, and that was during Obama's administration.

26
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:38,540
They didn't do a thing about that.

27
00:01:38,780 --> 00:01:39,700
They let it happen.

28
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:44,480
When I started farming, we had five or six Arkansas-based seed companies.

29
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:46,600
Monsanto, there's none.

30
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:47,740
There's none.

31
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:49,180
They're all owned by Bayer.

32
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:52,900
Point blank, they created a monopoly to poison you,

33
00:01:53,060 --> 00:01:55,160
and both parties are in on it.

34
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:58,220
Right now, there's a farm bill, H.R. 7567,

35
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:01,320
that Congress is expected to vote on this week

36
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:03,280
that codifies immunity for Bayer

37
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:06,080
and basically destroy organic farming going forward.

38
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:08,100
We cannot allow this to pass.

